    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the unequivocal anchor of the offense. With an elite efficiency score of 80.87, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against Roki Sasaki; the combination of a favorable park factor and a slow delivery from the mound\u2014which maximizes his stolen base potential\u2014positions him to capitalize on the scarcest category in our 5x5 format. Similarly, **Brice Turang** (68.84) and **Mickey Moniak** (68.23) are primary targets to drive production today. **Brice Turang** earns his spot at the top of the order against Zebby Matthews, while **Mickey Moniak** enjoys a massive platoon advantage (+14%) against Leahy, making him a high-upside play despite a slight park penalty.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved the marginal starters in the 40\u201350 range, specifically the choice between **Zach McKinstry** and **Cole Young**. While **Cole Young** was considered for the middle infield slot, he finished below the threshold at 35.20 due to the brutal matchup against Drew Rasmussen\u2019s 3.19 xERA and a poor park factor. **Zach McKinstry** (46.32) gets the nod by the narrowest of margins, though his value is capped by a difficult matchup against JT Brubaker and a suboptimal #9 spot in the order. Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the weather in the **Austin Riley** matchup; while he projects as a starter (51.76), the 38% rain risk is a flag that could lead to a mid-game replacement, especially given the density of better-projected outfielders in our ranks.\n\nWe remain thin in the infield due to the absences of **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**, all of whom remain sidelined on the IL. This has forced us to rely on higher-variance plays like **Max Muncy** (48.37) and **Isaac Paredes** (59.92). While **Isaac Paredes** is dealing with a significant platoon disadvantage against the lefty Robbie Ray, his base profile remains strong enough to keep him just under the 60-point \"Elite\" threshold. We will be tracking the lineups for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Corbin Carroll** closely; as these are all projected spots, any significant drop in batting order will require us to re-evaluate the risk of starting them against their respective arms.",
